# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — CODELAND
## A Professional 3D Minecraft-Inspired Java Learning and Adventure Platform

Act as a senior full-stack developer, 3D game developer, UI/UX designer, educational technology specialist, and game systems architect.

Build a complete, professional, interactive web application called **CODELAND**.

CODELAND is a gamified Java programming education platform. It combines structured Java lessons, interactive coding practice, story-driven gameplay, 3D voxel environments inspired by Minecraft, achievements, daily streaks, and leaderboards.

This must be a functional application, not just a landing page, static mockup, or visual prototype.

The application should look and feel like a polished commercial educational game.

---

# 1. CORE PRODUCT VISION

The main idea is to help beginners learn Java programming before entering an adventure game where they apply their knowledge.

The user journey must follow this sequence:

1. User registers or logs in.
2. User enters the CODELAND dashboard.
3. User opens the Java Learning Academy.
4. User learns Java concepts through interactive lessons.
5. User completes examples, exercises, and short assessments.
6. User unlocks the corresponding adventure level.
7. User enters a 3D Minecraft-inspired world.
8. User solves obstacles using the Java concepts they learned.
9. User earns XP, coins, badges, and achievements.
10. User maintains daily learning streaks and competes on leaderboards.

The key philosophy:

"Learn Java. Master the Code. Explore the World."

The platform must teach Java progressively. A complete beginner should be able to start without any previous programming knowledge.

IMPORTANT: The application must initially support ONLY Java. Do not add Python, C++, JavaScript learning courses, or other programming language sections.

